## Live account test

Bundle: `proof/live-2fa/20260819T230631.865433Z-0f69de279e82/`

- Result: PASS (`live_sequence_completed`)
- Login results: 454, 454, 455, 454, 454, login success
- Matching emails: 2; all four 30-second no-email windows passed
- Messages marked read: 0
- Credential or verification-code occurrences in the bundle: 0
- Bundle checksums: OK
- Govee device hardware: NOT TESTED

Two provider facts were established by that run and are encoded in this
branch: current mail arrives from `no-reply@govee.com` with a four-digit
code in the HTML body, and this IMAP server returns its highest UID for an
empty `baseline+1:*` range.

The generator that produced this bundle (`scripts/live_2fa.py`) is NOT part
of this PR. It lands separately so this change stays reviewable; the bundle
is retained here because it is the runtime evidence for this PR's claims.

### Coverage caveat

The live sequence ran at commit `0f69de27`. Review fixes landed afterwards.
Per change, whether the live run exercised it:

- Failed verification request now falls through to the 454 guidance rather
  than replacing it. NOT exercised live: all four requests succeeded.
  Covered by failed_verification_request_still_reports_actionable_2fa_guidance.
- Unknown delivery outcome (timeout, unreadable body) claims the suppression
  window; proven failures fall to the negative cache. NOT exercised live: no
  timeouts occurred. Covered by
  unknown_delivery_outcome_claims_the_suppression_window.
- Verification response bounded by Content-Length and truncated in
  diagnostics. NOT exercised live: real responses are a few dozen bytes.
- Suppression key derived from the lowercased email rather than client_id.
  This IS the mechanism the live sequence validated. Behaviour is unchanged
  (one deterministic key per account, still 15 minutes); only the key string
  differs. One-time upgrade effect: the entry under the old key is orphaned
  and expires on its own within 15 minutes, so a user who is mid-window at
  upgrade time may receive one extra email.

LIVE ACCOUNT TEST: OK (with the coverage caveat above)

