### Coverage caveat, round 3

NOT exercised against a live Govee account. The live sequence in
proof/live-2fa/ ran at 0f69de27 and every request there succeeded, so it
never hit a non-200 API status, an unreadable body, or a chunked reply.
These paths are covered by unit tests only:
  - non-200 API status  -> verification_response_rejects_non_200_api_status
  - no numeric status   -> verification_response_rejects_missing_or_non_numeric_api_status
  - accumulated-byte cap -> verification_body_cap_counts_accumulated_bytes

The HTTP-non-success path (status.is_success() == false) has NO direct
test: constructing a reqwest::Response needs an HTTP mock, and this repo
has no mock server in dev-dependencies. It shares its classification with
the two tested paths above. Stated here rather than implied as covered.

